# Branches to merge into "test/auto", one per line, in order.
# Order matters: earlier branches merge first, so put whichever branch is
# conceptually "upstream" (touches more core/shared logic) earlier in the
# list - later branches then merge on top of it, same as a stacked PR.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# This file is read from main, so changes only take effect once merged there.
# List your branches like this:
#
# feature/some-feature
# feature/another-feature

feature/add-counts-to-ds-section-nav
feature/device-display-group
feature/categorize-observations
feature/encounter-grouping
feature/hide-utility-resource-categories
feature/data-summary-filters